  "result": "I analyzed season 1's full-season yellowtail pattern by 20-day bins and compared it against season 2's data through day 121, then checked whether the upwelling-relaxation thesis actually explains the pattern.\n\n**Key finding:** the spring window is wider than previously tracked (good three_quarter/overnight ypa runs all the way to doy~180, not just ~120), there's a hard two-month summer dead zone (doy180-260) across every class despite favorable-looking SST/CUTI, and the standout opportunity is a sharp fall pulse at doy280-300 (day_1_5 ypa 3.557, overnight 1.182 \u2014 by far the best numbers all season). Critically, CUTI/BEUTI/SST don't cleanly discriminate the dead summer from the bonanza fall (both show relaxed upwelling), so I downweighted the upwelling thesis as a trigger and rewrote notes.md to prioritize reserving budget/PTO for the doy260-310 fall push while staying opportunistic-but-cheap through the spring tail and defaulting to inaction through the summer doldrums.",
